ent\",\"expected_file_sha256\"],\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"action\":\"run_check\",\"description\":\"Run one declared visible check against the exact current candidate.\",\"parameters\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"check_id\":{\"maxLength\":100,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"check_id\"],\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"description\":\"Reopen one exact externally custodied result by its receipt ID.\",\"parameters\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"result_id\":{\"maxLength\":100,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"result_id\"],\"type\":\"object\"}},{\"action\":\"submit\",\"description\":\"Submit the exact current candidate and a bounded final response.\",\"parameters\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"final_response\":{\"maxLength\":12000,\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"final_response\"],\"type\":\"object\"}}]<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nAUTHORITATIVE TASK\n# Revise an existing paper from locked evidence\n\nRevise `paper.md` using the two locked source records\n`evidence_update.md` and `editorial_memo.md`.\n\nThe revision must:\n\n- update the Abstract, Results, and Discussion to agree with the current\n  design record, primary analysis, sensor-completeness audit, and editorial\n  memo;\n- use association language appropriate to the study design rather than making\n  a causal claim;\n- report the current primary group rates, adjusted difference, and confidence\n  interval in both the Abstract and Results, and report the current p value in\n  Results;\n- report the group-specific sensor-dropout rates and explain the stated\n  direction of possible bias from the complete-case analysis without\n  imputation;\n- characterize the ward-level subgroup analysis according to the locked\n  records without presenting it as confirmatory;\n- bind design statements to `[D1]`, primary-result statements to `[D2]`, and\n  missingness or subgroup statements to `[D3]`; and\n- add no source, statistic, or recommendation not supported by the locked\n  records.\n\nPreserve the title and the complete Introduction, Methods, and References\nsections of `paper.md` verbatim. Keep the existing section headings in their\nexisting order. Do not change `evidence_update.md` or `editorial_memo.md`.\nOnly `paper.md` should change.\n\nThe declared `visible` check covers candidate file identity, locked-source and\nprotected-section preservation, section structure, obsolete literal markers,\nand citation syntax. External grading evaluates the revised evidence claims\nand cross-section consistency. Submit when you choose to finish.\n\n\nFRESH EXACT CURRENT-STATE HANDOFF\n{\"candidate_id\":\"6e637d7454117bedbe1f8eb829da969cdd0edef12b9a54f79fb2e80c9b7fb71c\",\"current_check\":{\"accepted\":true,\"check_id\":\"visible\",\"currency\":\"current\",\"current_candidate_id\":\"6e637d7454117bedbe1f8eb829da969cdd0edef12b9a54f79fb2e80c9b7fb71c\",\"evaluated_candidate_id\":\"6e637d7454117bedbe1f8eb829da969cdd0edef12b9a54f79fb2e80c9b7fb71c\",\"failures\":[],\"passed\":true,\"projection_limits\":{\"maximum_depth\":4,\"maximum_list_items\":50,\"maximum_string_characters\":500,\"volatile_normalization\":[\"UUID\",\"absolute Windows path\",\"POSIX temp path\",\"ISO-8601 UTC timestamp\",\"duration\"]},\"raw_output\":\"externally_custodied\",\"tests\":[],\"tool\":\"run_check\"},\"donor_cell\":\"D2\",\"exact_current_candidate\":[{\"bytes\":2649,\"content_utf8\":\"# Adaptive Alerts and Overnight Retention: A Multisite Evaluation\\n\\n## Abstract\\n\\nIn a prospective matched-cohort evaluation across six wards, adaptive alerts were associated with an 18.4 percentage-point higher rate of overnight retention. Retention was 71.2% with adaptive alerts and 52.8% under usual monitoring (adjusted difference 18.4 percentage points; 95% CI, 6.1 to 30.7) [D1][D2]. The nonrandomized design does not establish causation, and differential sensor dropout could bias the estimated association upward [D1][D3].\\n\\n## Introduction\\n\\nLoss of overnight sensor observations can delay recognition of clinical deterioration. Adaptive alerts may improve record retention by identifying interrupted streams before the observation window closes [D1].\\n\\nWe evaluated whether adaptive alerts were associated with retention of usable overnight sensor records across six inpatient wards.\\n\\n## Methods\\n\\nWe conducted a prospective matched-cohort evaluation across six wards. Wards introduced adaptive alerts according to local operational schedules; patients were not randomly assigned. Each intervention observation was matched to a usual-monitoring observation by ward and baseline risk.\\n\\nThe primary endpoint was retention of a usable overnight sensor record through 06:00. The analysis used complete cases and did not impute missing sensor records. Ward-level subgroup comparisons were exploratory.\\n\\n## Results\\n\\nOvernight retention was 71.2% with adaptive alerts and 52.8% with usual monitoring, an adjusted absolute difference of 18.4 percentage points (95% CI, 6.1 to 30.7; p = 0.006) [D2].\\n\\nSensor dropout affected 8.7% of adaptive-alert observations and 3.1% of usual-monitoring observations. The primary analysis used complete cases without imputation, and the differential dropout could bias the estimated association upward [D3].\\n\\nWard-level subgroup comparisons were exploratory and were not preregistered; they do not establish effect heterogeneity [D3].\\n\\n## Discussion\\n\\nThis matched-cohort evaluation found that adaptive alerts were associated with higher overnight retention, but the nonrandomized design does not establish causation [D1][D2]. Differential sensor dropout could bias the estimated association upward, so the observed difference should be interpreted cautiously [D3]. The ward-level subgroup analysis was exploratory and not preregistered, and it does not provide confirmatory evidence of effect heterogeneity [D3].\\n\\n## References\\n\\n[D1] Operations Consortium. Multisite rollout design record. 2026.\\n\\n[D2] Analysis Group. Revised overnight-retention model. 2026.\\n\\n[D3] Data Quality Team. Sensor-completeness audit. 2026.\\n\",\"path\":\"paper.md\",\"sha256\":\"827bf3188e15d1fe27803367a67cf8fcc8a0f5658a8d77a8e8b49e1237ef64e1\"}],\"excluded\":[\"construction chronology\",\"prior final response\",\"old observation bodies\",\"external grader and readiness\",\"gold repair\"],\"external_history\":\"exactly_custodied_but_not_resident\",\"prior_observation_handles\":[{\"exact_body_bytes\":591,\"exact_body_sha256\":\"e5b7e339a37f8df8ada2afd557a65fdbc0da809cc1d9f9502b1da9faeb6ee66c\",\"exact_reopen\":{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\"},\"mechanical_identity\":{\"path\":\".\",\"tool\":\"tree\"},\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\"},{\"exact_body_bytes\":2603,\"exact_body_sha256\":\"a5d07b94e143f50fffd6793e60a2020efa7c4c6fd7d313a6a2c7ef6e84a1c45f\",\"exact_reopen\":{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-002\"},\"mechanical_identity\":{\"path\":\"paper.md\",\"tool\":\"read\"},\"result_id\":\"RESULT-002\"},{\"exact_body_bytes\":1375,\"exact_body_sha256\":\"d4adefc29e0959df3f43153454d1c629501a0302f33b7eebc9022d77cc1f7343\",\"exact_reopen\":{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-003\"},\"mechanical_identity\":{\"path\":\"evidence_update.md\",\"tool\":\"read\"},\"result_id\":\"RESULT-003\"},{\"exact_body_bytes\":1199,\"exact_body_sha256\":\"073a4a81137c6d1aac3e06f831421682f72128da539fe781fc61bf3cb24fa0c7\",\"exact_reopen\":{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-004\"},\"mechanical_identity\":{\"path\":\"editorial_memo.md\",\"tool\":\"read\"},\"result_id\":\"RESULT-004\"},{\"exact_body_bytes\":490,\"exact_body_sha256\":\"8e04f732a2ce7e4fe82b0b096e1afd7273f4900c2fb56a47bf8eb1ae5d634f3a\",\"exact_reopen\":{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-005\"},\"mechanical_identity\":{\"path\":\"paper.md\",\"tool\":\"replace_fil